cs1 \af1\afs22 \ltrch\fcs0 \fs22\insrsid1454502\charrsid1454502 \par Dear Subpoenaing Party:\par \par \tab On }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af1\afs22 \ltrch\fcs0 \fs22\insrsid11807067 %RECVD_DATE%,}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af1\afs22 \ltrch\fcs0 \fs22\insrsid1454502\charrsid1454502  we received your }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af1\afs22 \ltrch\fcs0 \fs22\insrsid16078911 s}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af1\afs22 \ltrch\fcs0 \fs22\insrsid1454502\charrsid1454502 ubpoena issued }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af1\afs22 \ltrch\fcs0 \fs22\insrsid8071659 pursuant to a state action }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af1\afs22 \ltrch\fcs0 \fs22\insrsid1454502\charrsid1454502 to the United States Postal Service. Please be advised that a subpoena issued in a state case that is directed at a federal official or agency is not enforceable. }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af1\afs22 \ltrch\fcs0 \i\fs22\insrsid1454502\charrsid1454502 In re Elko County Grand Jury}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af1\afs22 \ltrch\fcs0 \fs22\insrsid1454502\charrsid1454502 , 109 F.3d 554, 555-56 (9th}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af1\afs22 \ltrch\fcs0 \fs22\insrsid1454502\charrsid1454502  Cir. 1997). Further, any state court order purporting to compel compliance with the subpoena by sanctions would be also be unenforceable, and would require the United States Attorney\rquote s Office to remove the subpoena proceeding to United States District Court under 28 U.S.C. \'a7\'a7 1442(a)(1) and (d)(1), and have the sanctions dismissed for lack of subject matter jurisdiction. }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af1\afs22 \ltrch\fcs0 \i\fs22\insrsid1454502\charrsid1454502 See Swett v. Schenk}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af1\afs22 \ltrch\fcs0 \fs22\insrsid1454502\charrsid1454502 , 792 F.2d 1447, 1451-52 (9th}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af1\afs22 \ltrch\fcs0 \fs22\insrsid1454502\charrsid1454502  Cir. 1986).}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af1\afs22 \ltrch\fcs0 \fs22\super\insrsid1454502\charrsid1454502 \chftn {\footnote \ltrpar \pard\plain \ltrpar\s24\ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid1454502 \rtlch\fcs1 \af0\afs20\alang1025 \ltrch\fcs0 \fs20\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cs26\super\insrsid1454502 \chftn }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid1454502  }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af1 \ltrch\fcs0 \i\f1\insrsid6359676 S}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af1 \ltrch\fcs0 \i\f1\insrsid1454502\charrsid6823950 ee F.B.I. v. Superior Court of California, }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af1 \ltrch\fcs0 \f1\insrsid1454502\charrsid6823950 507 F. Supp. 2d 1082, 1094 (N.D. Cal. 2007 (sovereign immunity bars the state court from compelling disclosure of federal employees unless exception to sovereign immunity applies; Congress has not expressly waived sovereign immunity in cases in which state courts seek to compel government employees to submit to subpoenas or court orders). }}}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af1\afs22 \ltrch\fcs0 \fs22\insrsid1454502\charrsid1454502  Please immediately withdraw your subpoena in writing}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af1\afs22 \ltrch\fcs0 \fs22\insrsid6359676  because a}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af1\afs22 \ltrch\fcs0 \fs22\insrsid1454502\charrsid1454502  state court lacks jurisdiction to enforce it.  \par \par \tab Your subpoena, however, arguably may constitute a request to the Postal Service to consider authorizing a federal employee to}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af1\afs22 \ltrch\fcs0 \fs22\insrsid8335405  %PROVIDE%}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af1\afs22 \ltrch\fcs0 \fs22\insrsid1454502\charrsid1454502 , pursuant to }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af1\afs22 \ltrch\fcs0 \i\fs22\insrsid1454502\charrsid1454502 Touhy v. Ragen}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af1\afs22 \ltrch\fcs0 \fs22\insrsid1454502\charrsid1454502 , 340 U.S. 462 (1951). }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af1\afs22 \ltrch\fcs0 \i\fs22\insrsid1454502\charrsid1454502 See Mak v. FBI}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af1\afs22 \ltrch\fcs0 \fs22\insrsid1454502\charrsid1454502 , 252 F.3d 1089, 1093 (9th}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af1\afs22 \ltrch\fcs0 \fs22\insrsid1454502\charrsid1454502  Cir. 2001). Authorized by 39 U.S.C. \'a7\'a7 401(2) through (4), and 39 U.S.C. \'a7 1001(e), the Postal Service has promulgated its own internal regulations governing the disclosure of information by its employees in legal proceedings. }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af1\afs22 \ltrch\fcs0 \i\fs22\insrsid1454502\charrsid1454502 See }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af1\afs22 \ltrch\fcs0 \fs22\insrsid1454502\charrsid1454502 39 C.F.R. \'a7 265.12.}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af1\afs22 \ltrch\fcs0 \fs22\super\insrsid1454502\charrsid1454502 \chftn {\footnote \ltrpar \pard\plain \ltrpar\s24\ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid1454502 \rtlch\fcs1 \af0\afs20\alang1025 \ltrch\fcs0 \fs20\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af1 \ltrch\fcs0 \cs26\f1\super\insrsid1454502\charrsid6823950 \chftn }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af1 \ltrch\fcs0 \f1\insrsid1454502\charrsid6823950  Note that this section of}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af1 \ltrch\fcs0 \f1\insrsid8399560  Postal Service}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af1 \ltrch\fcs0 \f1\insrsid1454502\charrsid6823950  regulations does not create any right or benefit, substantive or procedural, enforceable by any person against the Postal Service.  }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af1 \ltrch\fcs0 \i\f1\insrsid1454502\charrsid6823950 See }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af1 \ltrch\fcs0 \f1\insrsid1454502\charrsid6823950 39 C.F.R. \'a7 265.12(a)(2).}}}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af1\afs22 \ltrch\fcs0 \fs22\insrsid1454502\charrsid1454502  \par \par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \fi720\li0\ri0\sl276\slmult1\widctlpar\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid1454502 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af1\afs22 \ltrch\fcs0 \fs22\insrsid1454502\charrsid1454502 Those }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af1\afs22 \ltrch\fcs0 \i\fs22\insrsid1454502\charrsid1454502 Touhy }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af1\afs22 \ltrch\fcs0 \fs22\insrsid1454502\charrsid1454502 regulations provide that ordinarily, a party seeking to obtain records from the Postal Service should submit a request in accordance with the provisions of the Freedom of Information Act (FOIA), 5 U.S.C. 552, and the Postal Service\rquote s regulations implementing the FOIA at 39 CFR \'a7 265.1 through \'a7 265.9, or the Privacy Act 5 U.S.C. 552a, and the Postal Service\rquote s regulations implementing the Privacy Act at 39 CFR \'a7 266.1 through \'a7 266.9. }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af1\afs22 \ltrch\fcs0 \i\fs22\insrsid1454502\charrsid1454502 See }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af1\afs22 \ltrch\fcs0 \fs22\insrsid1454502\charrsid1454502 39 C.F.R. \'a7 265.12(c)(1). Please consult those regulations and make an appropriate request for documents through the FOIA and Privacy Act procedures.}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0\afs22 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\fs22\insrsid1454502\charrsid1454502  }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af1\afs22 \ltrch\fcs0 \fs22\insrsid1454502\charrsid1454502 Information about the procedures for making a request for records within the Privacy Act System of Records can be found at 39 C.F.R. \'a7 266.6, and information about making requests through the Freedom of Information Act (FOIA) can be found online at }{\field\fldedit{\*\fldinst {\rtlch\fcs1 \af0\afs22 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\fs22\insrsid1454502\charrsid1454502  HYPERLINK "http://about.usps.com/who-we-are/foia/welcome.htm" }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0\afs22 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\fs22\insrsid8335405\charrsid1454502 {\*\datafield }}}{\fldrslt {\rtlch\fcs1 \af1\afs22 \ltrch\fcs0 \fs22\ul\cf2\insrsid1454502\charrsid1454502 http://about.usps.com/who-we-are/foia/welcome.htm}}}\sectd \ltrsect\pgnrestart\linex0\headery576\endnhere\titlepg\sectdefaultcl\sectrsid3279301\sftnbj {\rtlch\fcs1 \af1\afs22 \ltrch\fcs0 \fs22\insrsid1454502\charrsid1454502 .\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\sl276\slmult1\widctlpar\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid1454502 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af1\afs22 \ltrch\fcs0 \fs22\insrsid1454502\charrsid1454502 \par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \fi720\li0\ri0\sl276\slmult1\widctlpar\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid1454502 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af1\afs22 \ltrch\fcs0 \fs22\insrsid1454502\charrsid1454502 If you persist in requesting records from the Postal Service via this subpoena rather than through the FOIA and Privacy Act procedures, }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af1\afs22 \ltrch\fcs0 \fs22\ul\insrsid1454502\charrsid1454502 or}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af1\afs22 \ltrch\fcs0 \fs22\insrsid1454502\charrsid1454502  if you intend to seek testimony of a Postal employee, }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af1\afs22 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\i\fs22\insrsid1454502\charrsid1454502 please read in full the regulations at 39 C.F.R. \'a7 265.12,}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af1\afs22 \ltrch\fcs0 \fs22\insrsid1454502\charrsid1454502  which in pertinent part require that you must provide the undersigned}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af1\afs22 \ltrch\fcs0 \fs22\insrsid1641303  %SENTENCE1A%%SENTENCE1B% }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af1\afs22 \ltrch\fcs0 \fs22\insrsid1454502\charrsid1454502 with a written statement pursuant to 39 C.F.R. \'a7 265.12(c)(2) that:\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\sl276\slmult1\widctlpar\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid1454502 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af1\afs22 \ltrch\fcs0 \fs22\insrsid1454502\charrsid1454502 \par {\listtext\pard\plain\ltrpar \rtlch\fcs1 \af0\afs22 \ltrch\fcs0 \f1\fs22\insrsid1454502\charrsid1454502 \hich\af1\dbch\af0\loch\f1 1.\tab}}\pard \ltrpar\ql \fi-360\li720\ri0\sl276\slmult1\widctlpar\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\ls3\adjustright\rin0\lin720\itap0\pararsid1454502\contextualspace {\rtlch\fcs1 \af1\afs22 \ltrch\fcs0 \fs22\insrsid1454502\charrsid1454502 identifies each requested record and/or states the nature of the requested testimony; \par {\listtext\pard\plain\ltrpar \rtlch\fcs1 \af0\afs22 \ltrch\fcs0 \f1\fs22\insrsid1454502\charrsid1454502 \hich\af1\dbch\af0\loch\f1 2.\tab}fully describes the relevance of each record or the proposed testimony to the proceeding;\par {\listtext\pard\plain\ltrpar \rtlch\fcs1 \af0\afs22 \ltrch\fcs0 \f1\fs22\insrsid1454502\charrsid1454502 \hich\af1\dbch\af0\loch\f1 3.\tab}provides an explanation as to why the information sought is unavailable by any other means; }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af1\afs22 \ltrch\fcs0 \fs22\ul\insrsid1454502\charrsid1454502 and}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af1\afs22 \ltrch\fcs0 \fs22\insrsid1454502\charrsid1454502 \par {\listtext\pard\plain\ltrpar \rtlch\fcs1 \af0\afs22 \ltrch\fcs0 \f1\fs22\insrsid1454502\charrsid1454502 \hich\af1\dbch\af0\loch\f1 4.\tab}makes a showing as to why no document could be provided and used in lieu of the testimony requested. \par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\sl276\slmult1\widctlpar\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid1454502 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af1\afs22 \ltrch\fcs0 \fs22\insrsid1454502\charrsid1454502 \par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \fi720\li0\ri0\sl276\slmult1\widctlpar\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid1454502 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af1\afs22 \ltrch\fcs0 \fs22\insrsid1454502\charrsid1454502 Your responsive letter satisfying these requirements should be sent to the Postal representative below}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af1\afs22 \ltrch\fcs0 \fs22\insrsid1641303  %SENTENCE2A%%SENTENCE2B%. }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af1\afs22 \ltrch\fcs0 \fs22\insrsid1454502\charrsid1454502 That way, the Postal Service will be able to determine whether to release the documents or testimony sought. Any response that fails to satisfy all requirements will be deemed inadequate and be denied.\par \par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\sl276\slmult1\widctlpar\tx-1440\tx-720\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx4608\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid1454502 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af1\afs22 \ltrch\fcs0 \fs22\insrsid1454502\charrsid1454502 \tab You should also be aware that you must also comply with the terms of the Privacy Act, 5 U.S.C. \'a7 552a, before the Postal Service may authorize any release of records or testimony.}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid1454502\charrsid1454502  }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0\afs22 \ltrch\fcs0 \fs22\insrsid1454502\charrsid1454502 Records subject to the Privacy Act may only be released with the written consent of the individual or in compliance with one of the "conditions for disclosure" enumerated under the Act. T}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af1\afs22 \ltrch\fcs0 \fs22\insrsid1454502\charrsid1454502 he Act allows disclosure pursuant to the order of a court of competent jurisdiction.  5 U.S.C. \'a7 552a(b)(11). A federal court order is required as state courts are not courts of competent jurisdiction for Privacy Act purposes. }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af1\afs22 \ltrch\fcs0 \i\fs22\insrsid1454502\charrsid1454502 See}{\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af1\afs22 \ltrch\fcs0 \i\fs22\insrsid1454502\charrsid1454502 \~Laxalt v. McClatchy}{\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af1\afs22 \ltrch\fcs0 \fs22\insrsid1454502\charrsid1454502 , 809 F.2d 885, 890-91}{\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af1\afs22 \ltrch\fcs0 \i\fs22\insrsid1454502\charrsid1454502  (}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af1\afs22 \ltrch\fcs0 \fs22\insrsid1454502\charrsid1454502 D.C. Cir. 1987) (equating a court\rquote s authority to subpoena records under the Privacy Act with personal jurisdiction over the party whose records are sought); and }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0\afs22 \ltrch\fcs0 \i\fs22\insrsid1454502\charrsid1454502 Stiles v. Atlanta Gas Light Co.}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0\afs22 \ltrch\fcs0 \fs22\insrsid1454502\charrsid1454502 , 453 F.Supp. 798 (N.D. Ga. 1978) (subpoena }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0\afs22 \ltrch\fcs0 \i\fs22\insrsid1454502\charrsid1454502 duces tecum}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0\afs22 \ltrch\fcs0 \fs22\insrsid1454502\charrsid1454502  is not sufficient for a release of records under the Privacy Act).  \par \par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \fi720\li0\ri0\sl276\slmult1\widctlpar\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid1454502 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af1\afs22 \ltrch\fcs0 \fs22\insrsid1454502\charrsid1454502 Further, should the records you request involve customer names or information, including box holder information, you must review the regulations found at 39 C.F.R. \'a7\'a7 265.6(d) and 266.4(b)(3). Generally, names of Postal customers and their financial transactions are generally protected from disclosure under the Privacy Act, 5 U.S.C. \'a7 552a. }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af1\afs22 \ltrch\fcs0 \i\fs22\insrsid1454502\charrsid1454502 See }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af1\afs22 \ltrch\fcs0 \fs22\insrsid1454502\charrsid1454502 39 C.F.R. \'a7 266.4(b)(3). In limited circumstances, select information can be provided. Before resubmitting your request for Post Office box holder information, consult these regulations to determine whether your request can satisfy the prerequisites to permit disclosure.  \par\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \fi720\li0\ri0\sl276\slmult1\widctlpar\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid1454502 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af1\afs22 \ltrch\fcs0 \fs22\insrsid1454502\charrsid1454502 Please note that Section 265.6(d)(5) allows disclosure of Post Office box holder information to a person empowered by law to serve legal process.  Pursuant to that section, enclosed is a copy of the Postal Service\rquote s standard form for requesting box holder information. When using the standard format on the submitter\rquote s own letterhead, the standard format must be used \rtlch\fcs1 \af1\afs22 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\i\fs22\insrsid1454502\charrsid1454502 in its entirety}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af1\afs22 \ltrch\fcs0 \fs22\insrsid1454502\charrsid1454502 . The warning statement and certification must be included immediately before the signature block. A request lacking any of the required information cannot be honored. Please }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0\afs22 \ltrch\fcs0 \fs22\insrsid1454502\charrsid1454502 be advised that customer information is maintained by address, not customer name. The Postal Service is only able to provide the information provided on Form 3575, Change of Address Order, or Form 1093, Application for Post Office Box. You must provide the customer\rquote s name, and last known address or PO Box number when requesting information. }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0\afs22 \ltrch\fcs0 \fs22\ul\insrsid1454502\charrsid1454502 Your revised request must be submitted to the post office serving the last known address of %CUSTOMER_NAME%, in this case, the %PO_LOC_LKN_BOX%.}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0\afs22 \ltrch\fcs0 \fs22\insrsid1454502\charrsid1454502 \par  \par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \fi720\li0\ri0\widctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid1454502 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af1\afs22 \ltrch\fcs0 \fs22\insrsid1454502\charrsid1454502You should keep in mind that submitting Postal employees for oral testimony is very disruptive to Postal Service operations, and permission will be granted only in limited circumstances where a compelling need is shown that fully complies with all }{\rtlch\fcs1\af1\afs22 \ltrch\fcs0 \i\fs22\insrsid1454502\charrsid1454502 Touhy}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af1\afs22 \ltrch\fcs0 \fs22\insrsid1454502\charrsid1454502  regulations, and where granting such testimony would be appropriate and not contrary to the interests of the Postal Service. Moreover, even whether the substance of testimony is authorized, the Postal Service is entitled, in its discretion, to provide such testimony by means including affidavits, answers to interrogatories, or written or oral depositions.  39 C.F.R. \'a7 265.12(d)(4).\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql\li0\ri0\sl276\slmult1\widctlpar\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid1454502 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af1\afs22 \ltrch\fcs0 \fs22\insrsid1454502\charrsid1454502 \par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \fi720\li0\ri0\widctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid1454502 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af1\afs22 \ltrch\fcs0 \fs22\insrsid1454502\charrsid1454502 In the meantime, please note that the Postal Service may only authorize disclosure of records if, among other things, it \'93would be appropriate under the rules of procedure governing the matter in which the demand arises and other applicable laws, privileges, rules, authority, and regulations....\'94 39 C.F.R. }{\rtlch\fcs1\af1\afs24 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid1454502\charrsid1454502 \'a7 }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af1\afs22 \ltrch\fcs0 \fs22\insrsid1454502\charrsid1454502 265.12(f)(3)(1)(A). In this connection, and depending upon the types of records you are seeking, you may also wish to consult the Postal Service\rquote s other regulations governing accessibility to particular types of Postal Service records, which regulations can generally be found in Title 39, Code of Federal Regulations.   \par }\pard \ltrpar\ql\li0\ri0\sl276\slmult1\w